afk: distribution default settings via $OMP_DISTRO_CONFIG.

Motivation: the afk wrapper used to symlink the generated distribution
config.yml into the profile's agent dir. That made the *user's* global
config a read-only Nix-store symlink, so nothing the user changed at
runtime (model selection, setup wizard state, any /settings write)
survived a restart — omp writes runtime settings to the global
config.yml, and the wrapper clobbered it back on every launch.

This patch adds a distribution-defaults settings layer: when
$OMP_DISTRO_CONFIG names a YAML settings file, it is loaded into a
#distro layer merged BELOW the user's global config (and above the
schema defaults). Precedence becomes:

  schema defaults < distro defaults < global < project < overlays < runtime

so the distribution ships opinionated defaults while every user-level
write persists normally and overrides them. Loading is lenient: a
missing or malformed distro file degrades to {} with a logged warning
instead of bricking the binary.

What must survive a rebase:
- #distro merged as the LOWEST config layer in #rebuildMerged (user
  config must always win).
- Both #load() and #loadReadOnly() populate #distro; cloneForCwd copies
  it (reloadForCwd only reloads the project layer and re-merges, so it
  needs no change).
- The distro file goes through #loadYamlIfPresent and therefore
  #migrateRawSettings, same as the global config. #loadYamlIfPresent
  returns a TAGGED YamlLoadResult (since 17.2.1), not RawSettings:
  unwrap `kind === "loaded"` explicitly. Treating the result as a plain
  object merges `{kind, settings}` as junk keys and the whole layer
  silently vanishes — which takes skills.customDirectories, and with it
  the entire Superpowers library, down with it (tests/distro-config.test.ts).

